entityDescription:
The Associa&ccedil;&atilde;o CCG/zgdv - Centro de Computa&ccedil;&atilde;o Gr&aacute;fica (CCG/zgdv Institute) was founded in 1993 and is a private, not for profit institute, integrated in the Portuguese Scientific and Technological System. 
CCG/zgdv is formally recognized by the Portuguese Government as a Public-Interest R&D organization, by the Portuguese Agency for Innovation as Centre for Technology and Innovation, and by the Portuguese Science and Technology Foundation as part of the ALGORITMI Research Centre (the first Research Centre formally recognized in Portugal in the ICT domain). 
It is an Interface Centre of the University of Minho for the digital economy, designing and prototyping new high-value processes, services and products in the fields of computer graphics, ubiquitous computing, human-machine interaction and information engineering. As an interface centre, the CCG/zgdv has a history of almost thirty years of partnerships with the Portuguese industry for the development and application of innovative technologies in its products, processes or services, allowing better facing the challenges of digitization. 
Today, technological development challenges include, further to the innovation, enhanced energy and environmental efficiency concerns, for which CCG/zgdvhas been contributing, by including such concerns in the specification, design and development of solutions in fields of application such as: 
- Software industry, ICT, and media; 
- Digital transformation in manufacturing and process industry; 
- Smart cities, smart mobility, and smart energy; 
- Intelligent building and environment; 
- Digital heritage, culture, and tourism; 
- eHealth and medical care; 
- Sustainability and Circular Economy; 
- eGovernment. 

The CCG/zgdv provides innovation services for the digital economy trough: 
- the identification of opportunities and needs for digital transformation technologies, as well as carbon reduction and energy rationalization; 
- the development of R&D activities under contract and collaborative R&D activities, in particular those leading to the emergence of innovative products, processes and services; 
- the support of technological prototyping activities; 
- the performance of verification&validation activities, accredited tests, trials, certifications preparation, including those required to obtain internationally the recognition of conformity 
- the transference and sharing of knowledge and performance of technological demonstration initiatives

